<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-clytia-hemisphaerica-turing-wavelength-s0-overall> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Clytia hemisphaerica Schnakenberg wavelength at 8.64 µm (Pass 2) — MorphoEval overall 87.4/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-27"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Pass 2 closes the Pass-1 probe defect. With the analytic eigenvector and a second-half fit, PDE growth rates match Jacobian σ(k) at Pearson r = 0.9993 and RMSE = 0.014 s⁻¹. Selected wavelength is 8.646 µm (assigned 8.64 µm, log10 = -5.063) at age 0 Ma. Equal-diffusion std(u) = 0.00132 versus wild-type 0.0193. Dv/Du from 10 to 36 increases λ_*. Segmented planula aspect is 3.23 against a circular null of 1, circularity 0.371, interior KS 0.191 against 0. CV similarity of the 12-frame 640 px GIF against the Momose micrograph is 82.1. A feathered outline was tried and rejected: it dropped CV to 60.5. Overall 87.4/100 (faithfulness 86.9, reproducibility 88.8); rubric morphoeval 0.1.0; checkpoint commit bd8176806dee28731b94a3866aa6609c1d9d4ba2; environment: . Dimension assessments: Model fidelity to source 90, Morphological realism / specimen match 82, Parameter expressivity 88, Morphometric validation 90, Source and data traceability 92, Code-to-model traceability 86, Reproducibility package 88. Output judged: docs/media/clytia_hemisphaerica_turing_wavelength_s0_growth.gif: rendered output of models/2026-delphi10000-clytia-hemisphaerica-turing-wavelength-s0.py at bd8176806dee28731b94a3866aa6609c1d9d4ba2, image/gif, 661371 B, 640×640 px, 12 frames, artifact_sha256 0f928ee2c59844b320c555aaa0a56e32593443151b4b7862a88b3a089a376e74 (sha256 0f928ee2c59844b320c555aaa0a56e32593443151b4b7862a88b3a089a376e74), spec_fingerprint 96a665cf0d7c09f92284588fc71976c4d562666ee4ba1270067ce2e4f5d4c878. Dual provenance: spec_fingerprint: 96a665cf0d7c09f92284588fc71976c4d562666ee4ba1270067ce2e4f5d4c878; artifact_sha256: 0f928ee2c59844b320c555aaa0a56e32593443151b4b7862a88b3a089a376e74; input_dataset_sha256: {datasets/clytia_hemisphaerica_turing_wavelength_s0/clytia_hemisphaerica_specimen.jpg=95bffe69b1854823..., datasets/clytia_hemisphaerica_turing_wavelength_s0/clytia_hemisphaerica_turing_wavelength_s0_reference.json=8e95bb9584ac6852..., datasets/clytia_hemisphaerica_turing_wavelength_s0/paper_citations.bib=045903087c0ddff1..., datasets/clytia_hemisphaerica_turing_wavelength_s0/scout_manifest.json=014d315226f357c5...}. Supersedes audit: 2026-10-27-clytia-hemisphaerica-turing-wavelength-s0-audit. Claim boundary: reported_in_source: Turing 1952 dispersion and Schnakenberg 1979 kinetics | Murray 1981 scale argument that wavelength count tracks domain size | Extant Clytia life cycle, gonad opsin, and hydrozoan ocelli as context; reconstructed_in_script: γ = 2.2268 s⁻¹ pins k_* to 8.64 µm at Du = 1 µm²/s and Dv/Du = 20 | Mode counts 28 (250 µm planula, reconstructed) and 231 (2 mm bell) | Render domain is the segmented planula mask; transfer_boundary: The 8.64 µm length is the assigned detail-tier anchor transferred onto k_* | The photograph is a planula; the ocellus is a medusa organ; does_not_claim: That a paper measured an 8.64 µm ocellus stripe in Clytia | Any temporal wavelength change (chronoseries 1/1, age delta 0 Ma) | That the synthetic species-gallery spiral is this specimen." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-rubric-0.1.0> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/overall" ;
    pk:hasScore 8.74e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

