        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/delphi10000-clytia-hemisphaerica-turing-wavelength-s0-5> ;
    dct:description "The simulation script(s) models/2026-delphi10000-clytia-hemisphaerica-turing-wavelength-s0.py implement the cited source model as published and produce forms that match real Clytia hemisphaerica specimens and the source authors' figures. A belief under audit, not a fact: its credibility is carried by the MorphoEval rubric assessments." ;
    dct:subject <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/main/models/2026-delphi10000-clytia-hemisphaerica-turing-wavelength-s0.py> ;
    schema:about "Clytia hemisphaerica" ;
    schema:additionalProperty "does_not_claim: Any temporal wavelength change (chronoseries 1/1, age delta 0 Ma)",
        "does_not_claim: That a paper measured an 8.64 µm ocellus stripe in Clytia",
        "does_not_claim: That the synthetic species-gallery spiral is this specimen",
        "reconstructed_in_script: Mode counts 28 (250 µm planula, reconstructed) and 231 (2 mm bell)",
        "reconstructed_in_script: Render domain is the segmented planula mask",
        "reconstructed_in_script: γ = 2.2268 s⁻¹ pins k_* to 8.64 µm at Du = 1 µm²/s and Dv/Du = 20",
        "reported_in_source: Extant Clytia life cycle, gonad opsin, and hydrozoan ocelli as context",
        "reported_in_source: Murray 1981 scale argument that wavelength count tracks domain size",
        "reported_in_source: Turing 1952 dispersion and Schnakenberg 1979 kinetics",
        "transfer_boundary: The 8.64 µm length is the assigned detail-tier anchor transferred onto k_*",
        "transfer_boundary: The photograph is a planula; the ocellus is a medusa organ" ;
    pk:anatomicalStructure "Turing pigment stripe / ocellus wavelength in Clytia hemisphaerica" ;
    pk:aristotelianEfficientCause "1. Chemical Turing / RD" ;
    pk:aristotelianMegistonGenos "II. Anaima (Invertebrata)" ;
    pk:aristotelianPoionForm "Stripes, Spots & Ocelli" ;
    pk:aristotelianPosonLaw "Turing Wavenumber k_c" ;
    pk:aristotelianSubalternClass "Zoophyta & Vermes (Cnidaria/Platyhelminthes)" ;
    pk:biologicalGenus "Clytia" ;
    pk:context "script(s): https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/main/models/2026-delphi10000-clytia-hemisphaerica-turing-wavelength-s0.py; output: docs/media/clytia_hemisphaerica_turing_wavelength_s0_growth.gif; organism: Clytia hemisphaerica; environment: n/a; claim_boundary: [reported_in_source: Turing 1952 dispersion and Schnakenberg 1979 kinetics | Murray 1981 scale argument that wavelength count tracks domain size | Extant Clytia life cycle, gonad opsin, and hydrozoan ocelli as context; reconstructed_in_script: γ = 2.2268 s⁻¹ pins k_* to 8.64 µm at Du = 1 µm²/s and Dv/Du = 20 | Mode counts 28 (250 µm planula, reconstructed) and 231 (2 mm bell) | Render domain is the segmented planula mask; transfer_boundary: The 8.64 µm length is the assigned detail-tier anchor transferred onto k_* | The photograph is a planula; the ocellus is a medusa organ; does_not_claim: That a paper measured an 8.64 µm ocellus stripe in Clytia | Any temporal wavelength change (chronoseries 1/1, age delta 0 Ma) | That the synthetic species-gallery spiral is this specimen]; phenomenon_size: 10 µm (1.032e-05 m, log10=-4.986 m, tier=4_cellular_10um); species_scale_ladder (10 runs from 10 µm to 3.1 cm): 10 µm:clytia-hemisphaerica-bioelectric-polarity, 38 µm:clytia-hemisphaerica-vertex-packing, 684 µm:clytia-hemisphaerica-turing-wavelength, 1.3 mm:clytia-hemisphaerica-clock-wavefront, 2.1 mm:clytia-hemisphaerica-morphogen-condensation, 2.7 mm:clytia-hemisphaerica-flux-canalization, 3.1 mm:clytia-hemisphaerica-elastic-buckling, 6.7 mm:clytia-hemisphaerica-branching-tree" ;
    pk:derivedFromPaper <https://doi.org/10.1007/BF00226774>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1016/0022-5193(79)90042-0>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1016/0022-5193(81)90334-9>,
